WITHIN-RUN COINCIDENCE ESTABLISHED: each run's own profile-speed
turnaround sits within one march step of that run's switch. The
cross-instrument statement upgrades: the coincidence holds run-by-run
inside the DNS alone. Honest structure in the offsets: inviscid runs
near-exact; all four viscous runs show s_turn ~0.2 BELOW s* -- the
transient turns around first and the inversion completes ~0.2 s-units
later, a consistent ordering (turnaround, then switch). The viscous
turnarounds also sit earlier (s~0.28-0.38) than inviscid (0.57-0.65);
reported as observed, unmodeled.

