(A) NU-GAP EXTENSION -- RESULTS AND ADJUDICATION (runs complete):
  nu=3e-6: -1.2112 / -1.1529, spread 0.058, both grids in the
    pre-registered band -> FLAT CONTINUES, letter-clean.
  nu=1e-6: -1.3657 / -1.2565, spread 0.109 (under bar). The 256-grid
    value is in-band; the 128-grid point estimate (-1.366) falls 4%
    BELOW the deep edge of the pre-registered band (-1.31), i.e. MORE
    inverted, away from the inviscid value; its CI [-1.55, -1.19]
    overlaps the band broadly. Adjudication per the pre-registered
    outcomes: NOT "flat continues" by the letter (band=OUT on one
    grid); emphatically NOT "crossover found" (the excursion is in the
    wrong direction for that); reported as measured, no forcing.
  NET: no approach toward the inviscid value anywhere down to
  nu = 1e-6. Any crossover toward inviscid now lies below 1e-6: the
  no-approach statement extends from two decades to THREE. The curve
  is flat-or-deeper across 1e-6..1e-3, every spread under the bar
  (0.016-0.115), deep windows n=19-27.

SWEEP SUMMARY: three ends attacked, three moved.
  (A) the nu-gap pushed down a decade: crossover, if any, below 1e-6.
  (B) turnaround-switch coincidence established WITHIN each run (6/6),
      with a consistent ordering: turnaround, then switch ~0.2 later
