VERDICT under the pre-registered rule: the deepening is REAL AT THE
128-GRID (replica reproduces it to 0.001; both cadences, 2/3 cuts) and
ABSENT AT THE 256-GRID (in-band, 0/3 cuts, both cadences). Combined
with the trend readout (monotone low-nu deepening on 128 only; no trend
on 256), the coherent reading is a RESOLUTION EFFECT: at nu = 1e-6 the
coarse grid's discretized trajectory genuinely deepens, the fine grid's
does not. Not sampling scatter; not continuum physics. nu = 1e-6 is the
128-grid's resolution floor for this observable; the continuum-facing
value at 1e-6 is the fine grid's in-band -1.22 (replica) / -1.26
(original), and the flat-curve statement stands there with a stated
coarse-grid caveat. The three-decade no-approach statement is
unaffected (every value on every grid remains deeply inverted).
Published quotes (nu >= 1e-5) are untouched by any of this.
